@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: chess analytics reads the same outcome enum the engine writes — it does not re-score a match
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no analytics store, tally, or chart types exist
'   under the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning UI
'   and persist modules before a covers: line can be honest.
'   outcome mapping it must wait on ..... _spec/_plans/forfeit-as-loss.puml
'   the kit for its widgets ............. _spec/_plans/chess-ui-primitives.puml
'   difficulty as a grouping key ........ _spec/_plans/chess-save-difficulty.puml
'   export as a fixture source .......... _spec/_plans/game-export-localstorage.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "analytics" is a READ MODEL over finished games. Wins, losses, draws,
' forfeits-as-losses, maybe difficulty. It does not decide a winner. If it
' re-scores, it will fight the engine the first time a rules patch lands.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   which charts, which time window
'   local-only vs a server
'   whether a running game appears
'
' Forfeit-as-loss has to land first or the tallies will treat a concede as a
' void and the dashboard will lie after the mapping changes.
title PLANNED — analytics is a read model;\nit does not re-score a match

database "finished games\noutcome enum · difficulty" as GAMES <<db>>
component "tally / read model" as TALLY <<app>>
component "dashboard widgets" as DASH <<app>>
component "**re-score in the chart**\nfights the engine" as RESCORE <<error>>
component "forfeit → loss mapping" as MAP <<app>>
component "primitive kit" as KIT <<app>>

GAMES ARROW_MAIN TALLY
MAP ARROW_MAIN GAMES : writes the enum
TALLY ARROW_MAIN DASH
TALLY ARROW_ERROR RESCORE
KIT ARROW_MAIN DASH

note bottom of RESCORE
  **Charts must not replay chess, because a widget
  that walks moves to decide a winner forks the
  dashboard on a rules patch.** Count the stored
  outcome enumeration instead of reconstructing
  it.
end note

note bottom of MAP
  **Forfeit mapping has to land before tallies,
  because counts built against a void will jump
  when concede becomes a loss.** Snapshot the
  dashboard only after that enumeration is stable.
end note

note right of DASH
  **Dashboard widgets come from the shared kit
  rather than a one-off chart treatment.** A third
  restyle of the same row is the failure the
  primitive plan exists to prevent.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. After forfeit-as-loss.** Confirm the outcome enum, then define the
  first tallies: games, wins, losses (including forfeit), draws, by
  difficulty if the key exists.
  --
  **2. Read, do not replay.** The dashboard binds to the tally. Export files
  can backfill, but a dump is a fixture, not a second scorer.
  ==
  **3. Use kit widgets.** Table and summary row first. Fancy charts are a
  later slice and still consume the same tally.
  --
  **Left open**: time windows; opponent grouping; whether tutorials count.
end legend
@enduml
